// J7 - a serialized ProductionLine instance comes back whole.
//
// Unlike J0-J6, this script instantiates NOTHING: it loads the instance committed under
// INSTANCES/lineL2.fml.rt and re-checks, on the reloaded instance, the business values J2/J3/J5
// prove in memory. The point is that federation survives serialization: the roles pointing into
// BOTH artifacts are restored, so every derived value follows.
//
// Regenerate the instance with ProductionLineInstanceGenerator (see src/test/java) after any change
// to ProductionLine.fml, production-line.xml or maintenance.xlsx that alters what it holds.
//
// Three defects had to be fixed to get here, all three worth knowing when writing FML that persists:
//   D1  a reflected model slot ("maintenance") is a live view over a foreign artifact and is never
//       serialized - only the reflected resource URI is. It is now rebuilt on demand through
//       ReflectedFMLRTModelSlot.reflectVirtualModelInstance().
//   D2  an XMLIndividualRole had no serializable identity: XMLModelSlot.getURIForObject() needs an
//       XMLURIProcessor, and textual FML has no syntax to declare one. Individuals now fall back on
//       a POSITIONAL uri ("xmlpath:/0/2" = child 2 of child 0 of the root). Simple, and deliberately
//       not robust: inserting or removing an element in production-line.xml shifts the path of
//       everything after it, and this instance must then be regenerated - which is exactly what the
//       xmlId assertions below would catch.
//   D3  XLSObjectActorReference now resolves reflected Excel instances by (concept, row number).
//       Those instances are rebuilt from the workbook, so they are NOT the same objects as before
//       serialization - only the row they sit on is stable.

vm = load -r ["http://openflexo.org/digital-twin-demo/FML/ProductionLine.fml"];
assert vm != null;

// The serialized instance. Its resource URI carries no INSTANCES/ segment: the resource center
// derives the URI from the resource name, not from the folder it sits in.
inst = load -r ["http://openflexo.org/digital-twin-demo/lineL2.fml.rt"];
assert inst != null;
// Cast required: load returns the resource data, statically typed FMLRTVirtualModelInstance, so
// without it "line.ligneXml" is rejected as an unresolved path element before the script even runs.
line = (ProductionLine) inst;

// --- Structure and both model slots ---
assert line.getEquipments().size == 6;
assert line.getMaterialLinks().size == 6;
assert line.ligneXml != null;
assert line.maintenance != null;

// --- The join still works, so equipments are addressable by code again (this is what collapsed
// when the XML roles were lost: "code" is derived from xmlElement) ---
conv = line.getEquipmentByCode("CONV03");
assert conv != null;

// Role 1 - the InternalElement of the XML. Asserting the DERIVED values, not just non-nullity:
// they prove the positional URI resolved to the RIGHT element, not merely to some element.
assert conv.xmlElement != null;
assert conv.xmlId == "EQ-CONV-03";
assert conv.code == "CONV03";
assert conv.xmlLabel == "TransferConveyor";
assert conv.type == "Conveyor";
assert conv.nominalRate == 950.0;
assert conv.vibrationThreshold == 4.5;

// Role 2 - its row in the "Assets" sheet
assert conv.assetRecord != null;
assert conv.assetRecord.code == "CONV03";
assert conv.assetDesignation == "Labeller transfer conveyor";

// Roles 3 and 4 - its readings and its maintenance operations
assert conv.readings.size == 14;
assert conv.vibrations.size == 7;
assert conv.interventions.size == 1;
assert conv.lastIntervention.type == "Preventive";

// The planted inconsistency survives as an inconsistency: in the XML, absent from the inventory.
eti04b = line.getEquipmentByCode("ETI04B");
assert eti04b != null;
assert eti04b.isInInventory == false;
assert eti04b.assetRecord == null;
assert eti04b.readings.size == 0;

// --- Topology: the MaterialLink graph is restored too, ends included ---
link = line.getMaterialLinks().get(0);
assert link.xmlLink != null;
assert link.source != null;
assert link.target != null;
assert line.getEntry() != null;
assert line.getExit() != null;

// --- And the transverse verdict, rebuilt from the reloaded instance alone ---
assert conv.isCritical == true;
assert conv.isBottleneck == true;
assert line.getEquipmentByCode("ETI04A").isCritical == false;
assert line.getTopPriority().code == "CONV03";
assert line.getActionablePriorities().size == 1;
assert line.getActionablePriorities().get(0).code == "CONV03";

log "Test PASSED: J7 - the serialized instance reloads whole, XML and Excel roles included";
